  items:
    - q: "Can I save a replay while I am streaming live?"
      a: >-
        Yes. Save important plays during your live stream, then insert them into the broadcast when
        you are ready. Your viewers can enjoy the replay while you keep covering the game from your
        iPhone.
    - q: "Can I play more than one replay in a row?"
      a: >-
        Yes. Add multiple saved moments to a replay playlist and play them back as a sequence. It is
        a simple way to create a quick recap during a break in play.
    - q: "Can I add transitions and a replay bumper?"
      a: >-
        Yes. Choose custom transitions between replay clips and add a replay bumper before the
        sequence, so the replay looks deliberate and fits the rest of your broadcast.
    - q: "Where can I find saved replays after the game?"
      a: >-
        Saved moments remain available in the replay library after the match. You can return to them
        when the game is over instead of searching through the entire recording.
    - q: "Can I share replays with parents, players and friends?"
      a: >-
        Yes. Export a replay to your iPhone Photos library and share it through the apps your
        community already uses, including messages and social media.
    - q: "Do I need a production crew to use instant replays?"
      a: >-
        No. Instant Replays are made for parents, coaches, small clubs and amateur tournament
        organizers who want a more memorable stream using an iPhone.
